Scope of this license
---------------------

Everything in this repository is Apache-2.0. Per ADR-13 the grant boundary is
drawn at the **repository**, not file by file, so no directory here is carved
out and nothing here needs a per-file licence header to be covered.

What that includes (ADR-8, ADR-13):

  - gurdy-proxy       interceptor proxy and the monitor actuator; the
                      local single-instance enforce actuator when it ships
                      (ADR-14 — it is not implemented today)
  - gurdy-verify      offline ledger verifier
  - the Transaction Identity Service, policy host, and decision ledger
  - the free starter policy set, and the adversarial corpus that gates it
  - the Gurdy SDKs (Python, TypeScript) and the shared conformance suite
  - gurdy-report, the free-tier local mini-report (BR-11)

Proprietary Gurdy components are distributed from a separate repository and
are NOT covered by this licence: gurdy-fleet (central ledger, fleet policy
distribution, fleet enforcement rollout/rollback, central attestation, SSO),
the agent-security and ai-governance policy packs, vertical packs, and the
**framework-mapped evidence reporter** (§5.6/FR-8 — the one that maps
decisions to NIST AI RMF / ISO 42001 / EU AI Act controls).

Note the reporter split, because the spec uses one word for two things. The
local mini-report in `reporter/` is free and is covered by this grant. The
framework-mapped evidence report is the paid artifact and is not in this
repository at all.
